<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/11th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Clontarf</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1014">1014</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Clontarf was fought on 23 April 1014 north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dublin">Dublin</a>. The army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brian-boru">Brian Bóruma</a>, high king of Ireland, defeated the king of Leinster, the Norse of Dublin and their allies from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orkney">Orkney</a> and the Isles, but Brian himself was killed. It was later remembered as the victory that broke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Viking</a> power in Ireland.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-clontarf.jpg" alt="Battle of Clontarf" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hugh Frazer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%27Battle_of_Clontarf%27,_oil_on_canvas_painting_by_Hugh_Frazer,_1826.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
